            <div xml:id="d636">

                <pb facs="0579" n="570" sameAs="frus:frus1940v02/pg570"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/4174c: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Consul General at Algiers</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Cole</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-06-24T19:00:00-04:00">June 24, 1940—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>20. In view of the fact that the Consulate in Tunis has destroyed its
                    confidential code it would be appreciated if you would telegraph the Department
                    any information that may be obtainable concerning the <pb facs="0580" n="571"
                        xml:id="pg571"/> attitude of Tunisia toward the war. Please keep the
                    Department informed also of similar developments relating to Algeria.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
